Z||000000||Cooter||01-17-2000||04:29 PM||||I know that street racing is a No-No, but I was driving my Iron Duck powered 85, so excessive speed was never a factor! A guy in his lowered S-10 with straight pipe/coffee can tip pulled up next to me at the light and really gunned it taking off, so I just let him go then and caught up at the next intersection. In John Force style, I watched the turn lane lights, when they went yellow I brought the beast up to 3,000 and did an amazing tire chirping launch. He was so embarrassed that he would not even pull up along side at the next red light. Wow, I actually ran something faster than that mail jeep that won't leave me alone and won. Oh, sweet victory. . .||||reg||1
