Z||000003||kornholio||01-17-2000||06:37 PM||||I'm new to driving a standard, so here are some stupid questions...<P>1.  To make the tires spin, do you let the clutch out quickly or slowly when at 3000 RPM?  The reason I ask is because when I'm driving a standard and I let the clutch out too fast in first gear, it usually stalls.<P>2.  Does it mess up the transmission or clutch if you do this often?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Patrick||01-17-2000||06:51 PM||||<BR>Waytago Cooter !!!<P>kornholio, if you rev your engine to five grand, and then floor it just as you pop the clutch, I guarantee that your engine won't stall. Of course, you'll be replacing your clutch and other assorted parts on a weekly basis... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000005||DRH||01-17-2000||06:56 PM||||Unless it's a 4 banger... then you'll be replacing the engine!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||01-18-2000||12:55 AM||||Cooter, I was in the same situation a few days ago! I was sitting at a stoplight in the right hand lane when a lowered late 90-s s10 comes up on my left just before the light turns green.  I didn't have any intention to race him, but I needed to get in the left lane, so I took off kind of quick. he was still moving when the light changed, but I guess he wanted to race, cause I hear his engine roaring over the sound of my stereo.  He closed the gap a little but I just stomped it and amazingly pulled away from him! I cut over in the left lane 'cause I had to turn soon and he just swerved around me.  didn't even look at me.  I was laughing my ass off.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  4 banger with a slushbox||||reg||14
Z||000007||stsmithgt||01-19-2000||07:12 PM||||Hey cornhole! you best learn how to USE a manual transmission before you go to ABUSE a manual transmission.  Dumping a clutch puts extreme force on your hole drive train.  The question is, which parts is going to brake first if I continue this pratice often?  Who am I to say? I blown up several transmission manual and automatic. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I had a ford with a C-6 auto in it.  The pressure plate shattered into eleven pieces.  I think that B&M shift kit I put in had something to do with it.  What a neck snapper!  It's an easy trany to rebuild though. ||||reg||1
